    "OP18-024 Kokoro is a useful alternative if you need a temporary way to set your Leader Active, or simply want a Blocker."
  ]},
  { title: "4 DON!! — OP18-031 Nico Robin", cards: [robin], paragraphs: [
    "This is your ideal play.",
    "Play OP18-031 Nico Robin to prepare your Leader's multiple attacks starting next turn.",
    "Her End of Your Turn effect sets your Leader and 1 DON!! Active. You can keep that DON!! available to defend your Leader with OP12-037 Demon Aura Nine Sword Style Asura Blades Drawn Dead Man's Game during your opponent's turn.",
    "Robin also protects your Characters from opposing Removal effects, helping you preserve important pieces."
  ]},
  { title: "6 DON!! — OP18-027 Zoro & Sogeking", cards: [zoroSogeking], paragraphs: [
    "This is one of the deck's most important sequences.",
    "Play OP18-027 Zoro & Sogeking for 5 DON!! and set 2 DON!! Active with its On Play effect. Together with the 1 DON!! you have left, you can attach 3 DON!! to your Leader.",
    "You can then attack once at 8000 Power, set your Leader Active with its ability, and attack a second time at 8000 Power.",
    "At the end of your turn, Nico Robin sets your Leader Active again.",
    "Zoro & Sogeking can also prevent an opposing Character with a Cost of 6 or less from becoming Rested, limiting opposing attacks or stopping your opponent from using a Blocker.",
