    "Choose based on your goal: increase pressure immediately with Double Attack or consolidate your board for the next turns."
  ]},
  { title: "10 DON!! — Set Up Lethal", cards: [zoro, luffyNine, gonbe, chimney, twinJet], connectors: ["OR", "OR", "+", "+"], optionRows: true, paragraphs: [
    "At 10 DON!!, OP16-035 Roronoa Zoro lets you get around your opponent's defenses.",
    "After playing him for 7 DON!!, you can rest an opposing card, then discard a card to attach 3 rested DON!! to your Leader.",
    "By adding the 3 DON!! you have left, you can make two attacks at 11000 Power.",
    "OP18-118 Monkey.D.Luffy is an alternative if you need to replace Nico Robin and find a reliable way to set your Leader Active again.",
    "Finally, if OP18-025 Gonbe and OP18-028 Chimney are already on the field, you can make your strongest offensive combination.",
    "With OP16-039 Gum-Gum Twin Jet Pistol and 9 DON!! attached, your Leader can make a first 14000-Power attack with Double Attack, become Active with its ability and make a second 14000-Power Double Attack, then make a third 14000-Power Double Attack thanks to Gonbe and Chimney.",
    "This combination represents up to six Life damage, but it is difficult to set up: your Searchers for Straw Hat Crew cards cannot find either Character, and both are vulnerable to Removal.",
    "Before committing to your decisive attacks, check for Blockers and opposing Active DON!! that could interrupt your sequence.",
    "OP12-037 Demon Aura Nine Sword Style Asura Blades Drawn Dead Man's Game can rest opposing Blockers or DON!! to help secure lethal, provided you plan for the resources needed to use it.",
    "The deck lacks card draw, so avoid sacrificing your entire hand for an offensive line that cannot realistically finish the game."
  ]}
];

