  { cards: [robin, sanji, zoro, gonbe, chimney], title: "Deck-Building Trade-Off — Consistency and Card Draw", paragraphs: [
    "The main trade-off in this list is consistency. Re-stand cards are necessary to make full use of the Leader, but they take up many slots in a deck that already lacks card draw.",
    "More flexible choices, such as Sanji and Roronoa Zoro, should therefore be evaluated according to how useful they are across different situations."
  ]}
